chine shop in north Carolina , where a friend of Rudolph <ei28 worked> . And nails <ei29 found> in the Atlanta abortion clinic <ei30 bombing> are identical to those <ei31 discovered> at Rudolph 's storage shed in north Carolina . A senior law enforcement source <ei32 tells> CNN , there is a lot of circumstantial evidence and it would be extraordinary to <ei33 have> all these bits and pieces and there not be a connection . And law enforcement sources <ei34 say> they ca n't <ei35 ignore> letters penned under the name army of god . Army of god is a secret organization that hates abortion providers , homosexuals and the US government . Army of god letters <ei36 claim> responsibility for the Atlanta abortion clinic <ei37 bombing> , a nineteen ninety-seven <ei39 attack> on a gay lounge and the Birmingham <ei40 assault> . An intense <ei41 manhunt> conducted by the FBI and the bureau of alcohol , tobacco and firearms <ei42 continues> for Rudolph in the wilderness of western north Carolina . And this week , FBI director Louie Freeh <ei44 assigned> more agents to the <ei45 search> . Freeh also <ei46 ordered> the <ei47 investigation> consolidate information under the Atlanta task force , another indication officials <ei48 suspect> a link between all the <ei49 bombings> . Privately , authorities <ei50 say> Rudolph has <ei51 become> a focus of their <ei52 investigation> . Publicly , they are <ei53 unwilling> to <ei54 make> any sweeping <ei55 assertion> . The reason , they <ei57 remember> Richard Jewell . pierre thomas , CNN , Washington .", "gold": [], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei4", "ei5", "ei7", "ei8", "ei10", "ei11", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei18", "ei19", "ei20", "ei21", "ei22", "ei23", "ei24", "ei25", "ei26", "ei27", "ei28", "ei29", "ei30", "ei31", "ei32", "ei33", "ei34", "ei35", "ei36", "ei37", "ei39", "ei40", "ei41", "ei42", "ei44", "ei45", "ei46", "ei47", "ei48", "ei49", "ei50", "ei51", "ei52", "ei53", "ei54", "ei55", "ei57"], "surfaces": {"ei1":